{
	title: 'Terminal output and redraw',
	spec: 'Items in the transcript are separated by exactly one blank row: trailing whitespace and newlines the model streamed at the end of a text or thinking block are not drawn, so [paused] after a cut-off answer has one blank row before it. Render transcript, streaming answer and prompt like a normal REPL: start at the current cursor without clearing, and leave the last frame visible on quit. When the frame first outgrows the terminal height, switch one-way to fullscreen mode per the terminal.md artifact (grow and full modes, never slice history to the viewport, scrollback is immutable). One tested width helper handles wide and combining characters and wrapping. Restore terminal mode on exit or crash. Test with a fake terminal. Lift the strings.ts artifact (width and wrapping) and its tests. A word wider than its row (a URL, an OAuth link) is never broken by the wrapper: it gets a row of its own that flows on at the full terminal width, first terminal row after the left pad, the rest from column 0, with no pad or fill inside it, written without CRLF between so the terminal soft-wraps it into one line that opens and copies whole; a change anywhere in such a chain rewrites it whole from its first row. Table cells and tool-output glimpses still break long words.',
